WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.490
Dr. Falconis selected three hardcover copies
of “Steve Jobs” by Walter Isaacson for

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:07.359
testing with the Clockworks.

00:00:07.359 --> 00:00:09.940
The first copy was placed on the setting 1:1.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:14.240
The output produced was a hardcover copy of
“Bill Gates” by Walter Isaacson.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:19.119
Upon investigation, the book was revealed
to be an in-depth biography of Microsoft founder

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.210
Bill Gates.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:23.260
The next book copy was placed in the machinery
on the setting “Fine.”

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:28.470
It produced a DVD that depicted Steve Jobs
narrating his biography in the style of an

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.470
audiobook.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.599
The final copy was placed on the setting “Very
Fine.”

00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:34.120
The output was a metallic cube with a single
button.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:39.080
When the button was pressed, the cube projected
a holographic image of Steve Jobs, which displayed

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:44.230
sapience and an ability to answer various
questions about Jobs’ life and Apple Computers.

